.TH ADA\-QUALITY\-SUMMARY 1 "" "ada\-quality\-summary 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ada\-quality\-summary \- read\-only reporting over Ada Quality assessments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ada\-quality\-summary
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ada\-quality\-summary presents the persisted quality status of the projects registered with Ada Quality: a portfolio overview, project and indicator reports, outstanding findings, review waivers, regressions, comparisons of chosen assessments, and historical trends, as terminal tables, Markdown, versioned JSON, or SARIF. It reads one coherent snapshot of the assessment database and never runs measurements or modifies the database.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B summary
Overall quality overview (default)
.TP
.B projects
Project status table
.TP
.B project PROJECT
Detailed project assessment
.TP
.B indicators
Cross\-project indicator summary
.TP
.B indicator ID
Detailed indicator report
.TP
.B problems
Outstanding quality findings
.TP
.B waivers
Review waivers in current assessments
.TP
.B regressions
Quality regressions
.TP
.B compare BASELINE CURRENT
Regressions between two chosen assessments (run IDs or aliases)
.TP
.B trends
Historical quality trends
.TP
.B history PROJECT
Individual project history
.TP
.B help [COMMAND]
Help and usage
.TP
.B completion SHELL
Shell completion script for bash, zsh, or fish
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-database " PATH"
Assessment database path
.TP
.BI \-\-format " terminal|json|markdown|sarif"
Output format (default: terminal)
.TP
.BI \-\-color " auto|always|never"
Terminal color selection
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Alias for \-\-color never
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " compact|normal|detailed"
Terminal and markdown layout
.TP
.BI \-\-width " N"
Override detected display width
.TP
.B \-\-include\-removed
Include tombstoned projects
.TP
.B \-\-enabled\-only
Include only enabled projects
.TP
.BI \-\-project " PROJECT"
Restrict collection reports to a project
.TP
.BI \-\-status " STATUS"
Filter by project status
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " KEY"
Command\-specific sorting
.TP
.B \-\-reverse
Reverse selected ordering
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Maximum result rows (0 means no limit)
.TP
.BI \-\-since " DATE"
Earliest history date (inclusive)
.TP
.BI \-\-until " DATE"
Latest history date (inclusive)
.TP
.B \-\-pretty
Indent JSON and SARIF output
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " CONDITIONS"
Exit 1 if regressions, violations, incomplete, or unassessed hold (comma\-separated)
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show help
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ADA_QUALITY_DATABASE
Database path used when \-\-database is not given; without either, .ada\-quality.db in the current directory.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables color when \-\-color is auto.
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Display width when standard output is not a terminal.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exit codes: 0 report generated, 1 report generated and a \-\-fail\-on condition holds, 2 invalid arguments, 3 reporting failure, 4 database failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ada\-quality (1)
